"""AQS-SAF-005 fire protection and detection (X-SAF-05, A-M-188; rev B X-FIR-01: sprinkler zone map,
pipe schedule class, fire-water tank and fire pump as drivers, graph fire params). Sprinkler demand
per level and zone (flow_graph/param/fire.py), water supplies, detection, special hazards, and the
API 521 fire case of the gas receivers carried from X-SAF-04.
Run: python3 docs-authority/_fire.py           (doc only, as the pipeline stage)
     python3 docs-authority/_fire.py --write   (also stamps params.fire on ROOF_TANK / CATCH_TANK; flock the repo design lock)"""
import json, math, os, sys
R = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))); os.chdir(R); sys.path.insert(0, R); sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(R, 'models/freecad'))
import params as P
from flow_graph.param import fire as F
from flow_graph.param import receivers as RC, pressure_nodes as PN, drivers as DRp
from flow_graph.param.sizing import relief as RL
from flow_graph.param.refs import cite
for k in ('NFPA13_2025', 'NFPA72_2025', 'NFPA20_2025', 'NFPA22_2023', 'NFPA15_2027', 'NFPA2_2026', 'NFPA855_2026', 'API521_2020', 'API520', 'NIST_WEBBOOK'): cite(k)
g = json.load(open('flow_graph/plant_flow_graph.json')); N = {n['unit_id']: n for n in g['nodes']}
rows, Vf = F.demand(P.PLATE_L * P.PLATE_W / 1e6); H = P.HYDRO
zs = F.zones()
sup = F.supply(rows, Vf, 9.81 * H['z_res0_m'])
md = ['# Fire protection and detection', '', 'Document number: AQS-SAF-005', 'Revision: B', 'Date: 2026-10-20',
      'Authority: AQS-PLAN-007 X-SAF-05 and X-FIR-01. Generated by `docs-authority/_fire.py`. Study; the fire engineer of record confirms hazard classes and hydraulics. Rev A A-M-188; rev B: sprinkler zone map, pipe schedule class and the fire-water tank and fire pump as drivers (`flow_graph/param/drivers.json` fire_* keys, NFPA13_2025 / NFPA20_2025 / NFPA22_2023).', '',
      '| Rev | Description | Date |', '| --- | --- | --- |',
      '| A | Sprinkler demand per level, two water supplies, detection, receiver fire cases. | 2026-10-16 |',
      '| B | X-FIR-01: hazard zone map (density/class per zone), pipe schedule class, fire-water tank and fire pump sized from the drivers basis; hazard class flagged pending the owner hall programme; graph fire params stamped. | 2026-10-20 |', '',
      '## Sprinkler demand (NFPA13_2025 density/area, Table 19.2.3.1.1 hose allowance)', '',
      '| Level | Occupancy | Hazard | Density mm/min | Area m2 | Sprinklers L/min (+10 %) | Hose L/min | Duration min | Volume m3 |', '|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
md += [f"| {r['level']} | {r['occ']} | {r['hazard']} | {r['density']} | {r['area']:.0f} | {r['sprink_Lmin']:.0f} | {r['hose_Lmin']:.0f} | {r['dur_min']:.0f} | {r['V_m3']:.0f} |" for r in rows]
gv = max(rows, key=lambda r: r['V_m3'])
md += ['', f"Governing: {gv['level']} {gv['hazard']}, {gv['sprink_Lmin'] + gv['hose_Lmin']:.0f} L/min for {gv['dur_min']:.0f} min = {Vf:.0f} m3.", '',
       '## Hazard zones (X-FIR-01; NFPA13_2025 class per zone, flagged pending the owner hall programme)', '',
       'Zones refine the level roll-up where the hazardous-area release sources (AQS-ELEC-009) and the hazard separation layout (AQS-SAF-007) make a zone differ from its level class:', '',
       '| Zone | Level | Hazard class | System | Density mm/min | Design area m2 | Sprinklers L/min | Hose L/min | Duration min |', '|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
md += [f"| {z['zone']} | {z['level']} | {z['hazard']} | {z['system']} | {z['density']} | {z['area']:.0f} | {z['sprink_Lmin']:.0f} | {z['hose_Lmin']:.0f} | {z['dur_min']:.0f} |" for z in zs]
md += [f"Zone classes and densities come from `drivers.json` `fire_zone_hazard` / `fire_nfpa13_hazards` ({cite('NFPA13_2025')} ch. 19 curves); the hazard classification stays flagged pending the owner hall programme (X-FIR-01 Done-when). "
       f"The governing zone demand equals the governing level (L0 EH1): {sup['demand_Lmin']} L/min sprinklers + hose.", '',
       f"## Pipe schedule and hydraulics ({cite('NFPA13_2025')})", '',
       f"{sup['pipe']}. Riser and feed mains sized at the governing {sup['demand_Lmin']} L/min at 6 m/s class: bore {math.sqrt(4 * sup['demand_Lmin'] / 60000 / math.pi / 6) * 1000:.0f} mm -> DN{math.ceil(math.sqrt(4 * sup['demand_Lmin'] / 60000 / math.pi / 6) * 1000 / 50) * 50} riser; "
       f"branch mains per zone at the zone demand on the same velocity class. The pipe-schedule method of NFPA 13 ch. 7 is not used: it does not serve extra-hazard occupancies and the L0 zones are EH1. "
       f"Hydraulic calculation from the riser through the hydraulically most remote area stays with the fire engineer of record (the {DRp.val(DRp.load(), 'fire_pump_head_margin_kPa')} kPa design margin of `fire_pump_head_margin_kPa` carries it).", '',
       f"## Fire water tank and fire pump ({cite('NFPA22_2023')} / {cite('NFPA20_2025')}, drivers fire_* keys)", '',
       f"1. Tank (gravity supply): {sup['tank']}. Primary: {sup['governing_V_m3']:.0f} m3 fire reserve held as dead storage in the bottom of the water tower, below the hydro outlet nozzles, so a hydro discharge can never draw it; static head at L0 {H['z_res0_m']:.1f} m ({9.81 * H['z_res0_m']:.0f} kPa), at the top life floor {H['z_res0_m'] - (P.Z_L2 - P.CLEAR_L1) / 1000:.1f} m. Refill of the reserve within {sup['refill_h']} h (`fire_tank_refill_h`, registered).",
       f"2. Pump (boosted supply): {sup['pump']}. Rated {sup['rated_Lmin']} L/min (listed step over the governing {sup['demand_Lmin']} L/min incl. hose allowance) at {sup['rated_head_kPa']} kPa (static shortfall + `fire_pump_head_margin_kPa`); churn <= {sup['churn_max_kPa']} kPa ({DRp.val(DRp.load(), 'fire_pump_churn_frac'):.2f} x rated, NFPA 20 4.16); runout {sup['runout_Lmin']} L/min at >= {sup['runout_head_min_kPa']} kPa (NFPA 20 4.18, 150 % / 65 %); motor about {sup['pump_kW']} kW at the gravity-assisted head, jockey pump and weekly churn per NFPA 25.",
       f"Two independent supplies per the redundancy rule: the tower gravity reserve and the CATCH_TANK suction source for the pump (the lower reservoir also takes the sprinkler run-off), so a fire after a hydro discharge still has a full supply in one of the two reservoirs (AQS-BLD-014).", '',
       '## Water supplies (two independent sources, redundancy rule)', '',
       f"1. Gravity: {Vf:.0f} m3 fire reserve held as dead storage in the bottom of the water tower, below the hydro outlet nozzles (NFPA22_2023), so a hydro discharge can never draw it. Static head at L0 {H['z_res0_m']:.1f} m ({9.81 * H['z_res0_m']:.0f} kPa), at the top life floor {H['z_res0_m'] - (P.Z_L2 - P.CLEAR_L1) / 1000:.1f} m. The reserve is split across the cells; each cell has its own fire outlet, so one cell drained for inspection leaves the rest.",
       f"2. Pumped: the NFPA20_2025 fire pump above draws from CATCH_TANK (lower reservoir, {H['catch_depth_m'] * H['area_m2']:.0f} m3 when full; it also takes the sprinkler run-off) and is fed from the critical bus with the genset as its second supply. It boosts the gravity supply where hydraulics need more than the static head.",
       f"The lower reservoir is sized to hold the hydro volume plus the fire reserve (AQS-BLD-014), so a fire after a hydro discharge still has a full supply in one of the two reservoirs.", '',
       '## Detection and special hazards (NFPA72_2025)', '',
       '| Area | Detection | Suppression |', '|---|---|---|',
       '| HAB, FARM | smoke detectors, NFPA 72 spacing; HAB sleeping rooms smoke alarms | wet sprinklers |',
       '| L0 shops, pyrolysis, oils | heat (rate-of-rise) and flame detectors at the reactor | wet sprinklers, EH1 |',
       '| Electrical rooms, rectifiers, inverters | air-sampling smoke detection | pre-action sprinklers (no water in the pipes until detection) |',
       '| ZNBR2 flow battery | smoke + H2 gas detection (purge basis, ess_tf) per NFPA855_2026 | wet sprinklers; the electrolyte is aqueous and not combustible |',
       '| H2 receiver CRYO_H2 | UV/IR flame + H2 gas detectors (alarm 10 %, trip 25 % LFL) per NFPA2_2026 | NFPA15_2027 water spray 10.2 L/min/m2 on the tube bank (exposure cooling); auto depressuring on flame |',
       '| O2 receiver CRYO_O2 | O2 enrichment detector (alarm 23.5 %) and flame | water spray as for H2; oxygen-clean (ASTM G93) |',
       '| CO2 store CRYO_CO2 | CO2 detector (5,000 ppm alarm) | water spray |',
       '| Cold box, L-1 wet process | heat detectors | wet sprinklers, OH2 |', '',
       '## Gas-receiver fire case (API521_2020, carried from X-SAF-04)', '',
       "Gas-filled tubes: A = F' A'/sqrt(P1), F' = 0.1406/(C Kd) (Tw - T1)^1.25 / T1^0.6625 (US units), Tw 1100 F (593 C), P1 at 121 % of set (fire overpressure). Liquid CO2: Q = 21,000 F A^0.82 Btu/h on the wetted tube area (drainage and fire-fighting present, F 1), relieved as vapour.", '',
       '| Receiver | Tubes | Exposed m2 | P1 kPa abs | T1 K | Fire area per half mm2 | Fire bore per half mm | Blocked-outlet bore mm | Installed bore mm (2 valves) | Depressuring release kg | Depressuring bore mm |', '|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
_dp = DRp.load(); _mg = DRp.val(_dp, 'press_design_margin'); _win = DRp.val(_dp, 'ely_window_h')
_RR = RC.design(_dp, g)   # R11 Rev AC regen: the receiver design/relief params were stripped from the Rev AC graph; rebuilt in memory from the same sizing modules, no graph write
for u in F.GAS_FIRE:
    c = PN.GAS[u]; p = N[u]['params']; des = c['P_bar'] * _mg * 100
    W = sum((e['rate']['value'] or 0) / (_win if e['from_unit_id'] == 'H2O_ELYZ' else 24) for e in g['edges'] if e['to_unit_id'] == u and e['presence'] == 'present' and (e['rate'] or {}).get('unit') == 'kg/d')
    P1 = 1.10 * des + 101.325
    p['design'] = _RR[u]; p['design_kPa'] = round(des, 1); p.setdefault('relief_mm', 3.3)
    p['relief_basis'] = {'P1_kPa_abs': round(P1, 1), 'T_K': c['T_K'], 'M_kg_kmol': c['M'], 'k': c['k'], 'Z': c['Z'], 'W_kg_h': round(W, 4),
                         'bore_req_mm': round(RL.equiv_bore_mm(RL.gas_area_in2(W * 2.20462, c['k'], P1 / 6.894757, c['T_K'] * 1.8, c['Z'], c['M'])), 2)}
for u in F.GAS_FIRE:
    p = N[u]['params']; ds = p['design']; fc = p['relief_basis'].get('fire_case') or F.receiver_fire(p)
    p['relief_mm'] = float(math.ceil(max(p['relief_basis']['bore_req_mm'], fc['bore_req_mm_per_half'])))   # governing of blocked outlet and fire case per half bank (as the write_graph relief stage propagates)
    md.append(f"| {u} | {ds['tubes']} | {fc['exposed_m2']:.1f} | {fc['P1_kPa_abs']:.0f} | {fc['T1_K']:.0f} | {fc['A_req_mm2_per_half']:.1f} | {fc['bore_req_mm_per_half']:.1f} | {p['relief_basis']['bore_req_mm']} | {p['relief_mm']:.0f} | {fc['depress_kg']:.1f} | {fc['depress_bore_mm']:.2f} |")
md += ['', "The fire case governs every receiver: the earlier 3.3 mm bore covered only the blocked outlet. Each manifolded half now has its own relief valve sized for the fire on its tubes (bore in the table, propagated to the graph relief_mm and the relief register). For gas-filled tubes API 521 warns that a relief valve alone may not prevent wall rupture in a fire, because the unwetted wall heats and loses strength while the pressure stays near set. The H2 and O2 banks therefore get automatic depressuring on flame detection to 50 % of design gauge in 15 min (API 521 5.20, wall 13.5 mm), sized in the table at twice the average rate for the initial peak, plus NFPA 15 water spray to keep the tubes cool. The depressuring vents go to the same safe-location vent stacks as the relief valves.",
       '', 'Open for the fire engineer of record: hydraulic calculation from the riser to the hydraulically most remote sprinkler, hazard-class confirmation when the owner hall programme issues, and the site fire-department connection.']
open('docs-authority/FIRE_PROTECTION.md', 'w').write('\n'.join(md) + '\n')

if '--write' in sys.argv:   # X-FIR-01: stamp the graph fire params (run under the repo design lock)
    for u, role in (('ROOF_TANK', 'gravity supply: fire reserve as water-tower dead storage'),
                    ('CATCH_TANK', 'pumped supply: fire-pump suction source and sprinkler run-off')):
        p = N[u].setdefault('params', {})
        p['fire'] = {'role': role, 'governing_level': sup['governing_level'], 'governing_hazard': sup['governing_hazard'],
                     'reserve_m3': round(Vf, 1), 'demand_Lmin': sup['demand_Lmin'], 'duration_min': gv['dur_min'],
                     'pump_rated_Lmin': sup['rated_Lmin'], 'pump_rated_head_kPa': sup['rated_head_kPa'],
                     'pump_kW': sup['pump_kW'], 'refill_h': sup['refill_h'],
                     'basis': f'AQS-SAF-005 rev B (X-FIR-01); drivers fire_* keys; NFPA13_2025 / NFPA20_2025 / NFPA22_2023'}
    open('flow_graph/plant_flow_graph.json', 'w').write(json.dumps(g, indent=2))
    print('graph fire params stamped on ROOF_TANK, CATCH_TANK')
print(round(Vf), gv['level'], '| zones', len(zs), '| pump', sup['rated_Lmin'], 'L/min at', sup['rated_head_kPa'], 'kPa')
